---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="VMTR01 Privacy Policy — Vireal" description="Privacy Policy for VMTR01.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">VMTR01</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: September 12, 2026</p>

    <p>
      VMTR01 is designed to record audio locally on the user's device. Audio recordings and their
      contents are not transmitted to Vireal or to analytics providers.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      VMTR01 may use Amplitude Analytics to collect pseudonymous usage and technical information
      needed to understand device compatibility, application reliability and feature usage.
    </p>
    <p>This information may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>device manufacturer and model;</li>
      <li>Android and application version;</li>
      <li>connected USB audio device characteristics;</li>
      <li>audio configuration such as sample rate and channel count;</li>
      <li>recording duration;</li>
      <li>operation success, failure and technical error categories;</li>
      <li>a pseudonymous installation or device identifier used for analytics.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data not collected</h2>
    <p>VMTR01 is not intended to send the following information to analytics:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>audio recording contents;</li>
      <li>recording filenames or user-created metadata;</li>
      <li>names, email addresses or account information;</li>
      <li>advertising identifiers;</li>
      <li>precise location.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Third-party processing</h2>
    <p>
      Technical analytics may be processed by Amplitude on behalf of Vireal. Analytics collection
      is configured to minimize unnecessary identifiers and technical properties.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, please contact the developer through
      <a href="https://github.com/vireal01">GitHub</a> until a dedicated support address is published.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
